Z||000002||Eric||02-03-2000||08:28 PM||||I'd say the Camaro engine installed in a Fiero is good for atleast 2,000,000 horsepower.  It may sound like a lot, but you have to take into account driveline losses in the Fiero will be significantly less than if the motor was installed in the Camaro.  Seriously though, you really never know exactly what kind of power a motor is going to make.  I think the motor is said to be around 210 hp from the factory, but of those factory stock cars, some will be fast and some will be dogs.  I could say a 3.2 will make 200 horsepower, but it's just a guess.  "Do what you can" should be the motto for tuner/modifier.  If you have money coming out the wazu, go crazy!  Buy a jet engine and strap it to the back of your car.  And if you have car knowlege and a lot free time, you can suprise yourself and everyone else with your creation.||||reg||10
