Z||000004||olympic||02-04-2000||12:01 AM||||   The 3800 Series II(1996 and up, I think)  used in FWD applications was rated at 205 Hp and would be a much easier swap than the camaro version.||||reg||1
Z||000005||batboy||02-04-2000||01:06 AM||||Yes, the newer the engine, the more ECM and wiring nightmares you'll have. I took the liberty of lifting these HP figures from the ACE website.<P>Versions of the 3800 Engine (Only Fuel Injected Listed)<P>1986 to 1991 Normally Aspirated Engine - 150 HP. Vin Code - C<P>1990 to 1995 Normally Aspirated Engine - 170 HP. Vin Code - L<P>1995 to Current - Normally Aspirated Engine - 205 HP. Vin Code - K<P>1991 to 1993 Supercharged - 205 HP. Vin Code - 1<P>1994 to 1995 Supercharged - 225 HP. Vin Code - 1<P>1996 to Current Supercharged - 250 HP. Vin Code - 1||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||02-04-2000||03:17 PM||||96-00 VIN code 1 3800 Supercharger's are rated 240HP not 250HP. This is from GM.<P>VIN code 3's and B's are rated 160HP (80's).<P>3's have roller cams. Not sure about the B's.<P>TK<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 02-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Phil||02-04-2000||07:05 PM||||I know for a fact that a '97 Series II S/C with an undersize pulley will give 222(221.7)HP and 273 ft-lbs Torque to the rear wheels. Allowing for a 20% loss thru the drive train that yields 277 at the flywheel. I know I'm crowing again but I just got it back from the painter and I'm waiting for the roads to dry.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Formula||02-04-2000||09:00 PM||||okay, I got something in my head now.....<P>The 3.4 TDC has 210 hoorses and 215 lbs thq, if the 3.8 only has 205 then I think the the 3.4 would be a lot more enjoyable because it revs to 7 grand (might feel like an indy car), (like the honda S2000!!!), BUT I've hear the 3.8 is a much more reliable motor then the tdc, soooooooooooooooo as long as you use oil with dialkyldithiophosphate in it, WHAT WOULD YOU CHOOSE??????||||reg||1
Z||000009||terryk||02-04-2000||11:44 PM||||For street drags, the 3800 wins hands down in my opinion. Torque right off the line. I've driven a DOHC Fiero and while the DOHC hauls above 3000 RPM, the Buick NA would kill it off the line. <P>But again, the DOHC sounds Indy-ish. It sounds like a massive sewing machine. A very nice sound indeed!<P>TK||||reg||1
